check:

he clue is:

  "param": "tools"

  If the problem were the Image API model field, the bad param would usually point at model. In the Responses API, official examples use a main model at the top level and only this
  tool shape:

  const response = await openai.responses.create({
    model: "gpt-5.5",
    input: "Generate an image of ...",
    tools: [{ type: "image_generation" }],
  });

  For direct image generation, use the Images API and put gpt-image-2 in images.generate:

  const result = await openai.images.generate({
    model: "gpt-image-2",
    prompt: "A children's book drawing of a veterinarian...",
  });

  Or curl:

  curl -X POST "https://api.openai.com/v1/images/generations" \
    -H "Authorization: Bearer $OPENAI_API_KEY" \
    -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
    -d '{
      "model": "gpt-image-2",
      "prompt": "A children’s book drawing of a veterinarian..."
    }'

  So fix one of these:

  tools: [{
    type: "image_generation",
  - model: "gpt-image-2"
  }]

  or switch to:

  openai.images.generate({ model: "gpt-image-2", prompt })
